{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551569-yang-yin-prana-stats","id":1551569,"title":"Yang / Yin Prana stats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-10T12:51:12-07:00","id":1551569,"title":"Yang / Yin Prana stats","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Is there any errata for the required attributes for Yin and Yang Prana? I ask because the core book goes:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yin Prana p.106 Kindred of the East Corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with<br /> the Yang Prana, the Yin Prana is a complicated endeavor; a<br /> student may raise his level in this Discipline <b>no higher than the<br /> lower of his Perception and Stamina ratings.\u200b</b></div> </div> </div> </div>But the Bone Flowers Dharma book goes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suggested Traits p.53 Bone Flowers Dharma book</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost all Bone Flowers should have at least <b>two<br /> dots in Dexterity in order to properly execute the Yin<br /> Prana</b> so central to their outlook.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is the Dharmabook wrong? Is the Corebook errated somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T00:07:13-07:00","id":1551583,"title":"","content":"As far as I know there was no errata on the <b>Yin Prana</b><br /> The two are not in a contradiction actually<br /> The Core tells you what you must have, what limits the levele of Yin Prana<br /> The Dharma book tells you what you *should* have but not what you need; it is a flavor thing - at least I always interpreted as a flawor thing, since it a suggested trait not a must have, but should have<br /> Like Yang Prana, Yin Prana relies on motions and postures to utilize the various powers, but these motions are a far cry from the frenzied katas of the Yang Prana. Yin Prana motions are slow, graceful and deliberate<br /> Both Prana are actually a series of increasingly more difficult forms and postures, which gradually allow a vampire to channel more and more of his Chi, be it yin or yang chi<br /> While Yin Prana is <b>Perception / Stamina</b>\u200b based to reflect the slow and calm, graceful and focused forms and postures and don't actuall requires a dextery roll<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Shrouded Moon</b>\u200b - no roll at all<br /> <b>\u2022 \u2022 Yin Mantle</b>\u200b - no roll at all<br /> <b>\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Bone Dance</b>\u200b - Through a series of slow, languorous mudras and postures, the vampire focuses her Yin energy into a series of concentrated waves that permeate the surrounding area. To perform the Dance successfully, the vampire must roll Stamina + Athletics (difficulty 7). For each success, the Dance must be performed for one turn, cumulatively. Once the vampire reaches the maximum effect desired, the vampire must continue to perform the Bone Dance, but no further Yin need be spent.<br /> <b>\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Eightfold Yin Mantle</b>\u200b - no roll at all, unless you want to craft insanely small and complicated things like a yin bullet...<br /> <b>\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Semblance of the Ebon Dragon</b>\u200b - The vampire concentrates for a turn, then spends three Yin points and rolls Ying + Rituals against the difficulty of the local Shroud<br /> <br /> This is not that different from the <b>Yang</b> <b>Prana</b><br /> Yang Prana requires great vigor and flexibility; thus it limited by Dexterity, or Stamina.<br /> While the Yin Parana is based on slow, graceful and deliberate motins and form, Yang Prana is a series of frenzied katas - reflected in the Dexterity/Stamina limit<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Principle of Motion</b>\u200b - no roll at all<br /> <b>\u2022 \u2022 </b>\u200b<b>Yang Mantle</b>\u200b - no rol lat all<br /> <b>\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Dragon Dance</b>\u200b - no roll at all<br /> <b>\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Eightfold Yang Mantle</b>\u200b - no roll at all but by rolling Wits + Crafts (Chi-shaping), she may mold the animus around her, shaping it into whatever form she desires and, thus, effectively cloaking herself in an illusion. The difficulty of the roll is based on the complexity of the desired shape<br /> <b>\u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 Semblance of the Scarlet Queen</b>\u200b - The vampire concentrates for a turn, then spends three Yang points and rolls Yang + Rituals against the difficulty of the local Wall<br /> <br /> Since the Pranas are katas, dance, motion - just in the Yang case it is like a crimson tornado, energetic, frenzied, quick and insanse, fluid adcrobatics and in the Yin it is slow, calm, serene - the <b>suggested</b> trait, what a Kuai jin <b>should have </b>I think is purely flavor to reflect she can &quot;dance&quot; and practiced these katas but not a requirement<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}